+ *           spawn_process_inproc
+ *
+ * Crossover-IOS fork, patch series 0003 (in progress): launch the child in
+ * the SAME host process — a new pproc thread group loading the child PE into
+ * the shared address space and running its ntdll init on the already-
+ * connected `socketfd` — instead of fork/exec. iOS forbids fork/exec, so this
+ * is the only viable backend there.
+ *
+ * The server-side setup (new_process/new_thread, socket handoff) is done by
+ * the caller and works in-process already (proven by wineforge exp. 004), so
+ * only this function changes versus the fork backend. The substantive pieces
+ * — per-pseudo-process PEB/TEB, in-address-space PE mapping, and the child
+ * init_first_thread on `socketfd` — are staged as 0003b–d in
+ * docs/DESIGN-0003-inproc-spawn.md. Until they land this backend is a wired
+ * but unimplemented seam.
+ */
